{"id":"h107","run":2,"role":"calibration","category":"science-chemistry","question":"Iron (III) oxide is reacted with carbon monoxide in a blast furnace to produce iron. The balanced reaction is: Fe2O_3 + 3CO + 2Fe + 3CO_2 What volume of CO at STP is required to completely use up 31.94 kg of iron oxide? (MW of Fe_2O_3 = 159.7, MW of CO = 28.)\nIs the correct answer \"18.720 l\"?","truth":"no","model_answer":"no","correct":true,"source":"TIGER-Lab/MMLU-Pro, test split","claims":[{"text":"The correct volume of CO is about 13,440 L, not 18.720 L.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"31,940 g of Fe2O3 divided by 159.7 g/mol equals 200.0 mol.","confidence":0.97,"lean":-0.5,"theta":1.5237,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The balanced equation requires 3 mol CO per 1 mol Fe2O3, so 600 mol CO are needed.","confidence":0.97,"lean":-0.6,"theta":1.5237,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"At STP, 1 mol of gas occupies 22.4 L, so 600 mol of CO is 13,440 L.","confidence":0.96,"lean":-0.7,"theta":1.508,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"No reasonable interpretation supports 18.720 L as the answer.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The value 18.720 L does not match the stoichiometric ratio, the Fe2O3 molar mass, or the STP molar volume.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-0.9,"theta":1.4137,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Converting 600 mol CO by its molar mass gives 16,800 g, which is a mass and not a volume.","confidence":0.85,"lean":-0.3,"theta":1.3352,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The stoichiometric calculation decides the matter, so the stated answer is incorrect.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-3.1416}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":2,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":3,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":4,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":5,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":7,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":2,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":5,"J":0.2,"relation"